{"name":"Golden Griffon","hex":"#a99058","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"griffon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of griffin (mythical creature)","A breed of dog usually called the Brussels griffon, reminiscent of the mythical creature."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/griffon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Griffon (roller coaster)","blocks":[{"text":"Griffon is a steel roller coaster located at Busch Gardens Williamsburg amusement park in James City County, Virginia, United States. Designed by Bolliger & Mabillard (B&M), the Dive Coaster model opened to the public on May 18, 2007. It climbs to a height of 205 feet (62 m) and reaches a maximum speed of 71 mph (114 km/h). It features two Immelmann loops, a splashdown, two vertical drops, and was the first B&M Dive Coaster to use floorless trains. Griffon was well-received by media and enthusiasts, and it placed third in 2007 in the category of Best New Ride polled by Amusement Today for their annual Golden Ticket Awards. Since its debut, it has also consistently ranked in the top 50 among steel roller coasters worldwide in the same annual publication, peaking at #19 in 2010."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Griffon_First_Drop.jpg/330px-Griffon_First_Drop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Griffon_(roller_coaster)","wikidata":"Q1546634"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Griffon_Splash.jpg/500px-Griffon_Splash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Griffon_Splash.jpg/1280px-Griffon_Splash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Griffon_Splash.jpg/500px-Griffon_Splash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One of Griffon's trains passing through the splashdown element","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGriffon_Splash.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Multiple_rows_of_golden_statues_of_the_Buddha_seated_with_flowers%2C_at_Wat_Phou_Salao%2C_Pakse%2C_Laos.jpg/500px-Multiple_rows_of_golden_statues_of_the_Buddha_seated_with_flowers%2C_at_Wat_Phou_Salao%2C_Pakse%2C_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Multiple_rows_of_golden_statues_of_the_Buddha_seated_with_flowers%2C_at_Wat_Phou_Salao%2C_Pakse%2C_Laos.jpg/500px-Multiple_rows_of_golden_statues_of_the_Buddha_seated_with_flowers%2C_at_Wat_Phou_Salao%2C_Pakse%2C_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMultiple_rows_of_golden_statues_of_the_Buddha_seated_with_flowers%2C_at_Wat_Phou_Salao%2C_Pakse%2C_Laos.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Fountain_pen_writing_%28literacy%29.jpg/500px-Fountain_pen_writing_%28literacy%29.jpg?utm_source